<title>POLAND: POLAND'S GDYNIA SHIPYARD TO GET $21.5 MLN CREDIT.</title>
<headline>POLAND'S GDYNIA SHIPYARD TO GET $21.5 MLN CREDIT.</headline>
<dateline>GDANSK, Poland 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Gdynia shipyard will sign on Thursday a $21.5 million credit agreement with a consortium of Polish banks led by the state-owned commercial Bank Zachodni SA, the shipyard said in a Wednesday statement.</p>
<p>The money will be used to finance the construction of a container ship for Germany's Alfa Ship.</p>
<p>Of the five bank consortium Bank Zachodni will put up 20.2 percent of the sum, Kredyt Bank 34.9 percent, Polish Investment Bank 13.8 percent, Bank Przemyslowo-Handlowy 27.4 percent and Amerbank 3.7 percent.</p>
<p>-- Ryszard Wesolowski +48 22 653 9700</p>
